@startuml new-starts-states
' cumin works - the state of cumin itself for new starts (quota). Q1 to Q4 of issue-states.md
' are transitions of this machine, not of an issue.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "starting new work" as Starting
Starting : do / cumin starts ready issues when it has a free slot

state "new starts stopped" as Stopped
Stopped : do / cumin lets the runs that go on end,\nand starts nothing new

[*] --> Starting
Starting --> Stopped : Q1 [cumin reads a quota window at its limit,\nor cannot read the usage]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Stopped --> Starting : Q2 the Owner allows the 5h window\n[the weekly window is under its limit]
Stopped --> Starting : Q3 [the time of cumin's next try passed,\nboth windows are under their limit]

note "Q4, in both states: [nothing can go on without the Owner,\nno agent runs] / cumin tells the Owner once that it waits." as Q4

legend right
  This machine has one instance for one cumin, not one for each issue.
  It lives on the Host (the latest quota reading of cumin), not on GitHub.
endlegend

@enduml
